{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/464357-feral-infection-radius","id":464357,"title":"Feral Infection Radius","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-01T00:01:39-07:00","id":464357,"title":"Feral Infection Radius","content":"I've been reading the entry on Feral Infection under Animalism and the only indicator of range I can find is anything that can smell the blood. Humans have a pretty paltry sense of smell so unless it's a lot of blood, that might not be very far. Any ideas? Should it be within BP range? Further? How about vampires? As far as they can auto-smell blood plus successes on a Wits + Composure check?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T08:48:36-07:00","id":464716,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it seems to just be smell, so it's going to vary a lot for different animals. Personally, I'd say humans within the same room, vampires within their smell range for their Kindred Senses. Anything else, you kind of have to estimate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-